WEBVTT

01:12.500 --> 01:15.740
Counting Haniwa's girlfriend,
he's claimed thirteen victims.

01:15.740 --> 01:18.140
That's a nice number, I guess.

01:18.140 --> 01:20.910
Still, it's a shame about Jin.

01:20.910 --> 01:24.480
It couldn't be helped.
He was meant to be disposable.

01:24.480 --> 01:29.850
I just hope we don't have trouble because
the music is incomplete.

01:30.120 --> 01:36.120
In the end, the public supports us
for opposing the Phantom.

01:36.120 --> 01:39.160
We managed to quell that little rebellion too.

01:39.160 --> 01:43.390
If only we'd managed to get rid
of the real Phantom too.

01:44.300 --> 01:49.040
I hear there's some unrest brewing within
the military. What's our plan?

01:49.040 --> 01:51.610
I'll take care of it.

01:51.610 --> 01:53.400
I appreciate that.

01:54.780 --> 01:57.370
Now, about that visitor...

01:58.250 --> 02:00.420
Arcade Van Vogout...

02:00.420 --> 02:05.720
He fought in the South Asian War, but beyond
that, nobody knows anything about him.

02:06.520 --> 02:10.480
Could it be that BG is onto our plan?

02:11.690 --> 02:13.420
Hmm...

02:16.460 --> 02:21.230
Eighth Night
The Maiden Whispers
in the Moonlight

02:41.920 --> 02:44.660
Hmm...Experimental art, perhaps?

02:44.660 --> 02:48.790
No, looks like he took these secretly from
inside the White Bell compound.

02:49.330 --> 02:51.000
Hey, what do you make of this?

02:51.000 --> 02:52.270
Hmm?

02:52.270 --> 02:57.140
Hmm, this is the dam, so this must be...

02:57.140 --> 03:01.140
The White Bell shrine in the middle
of the dam reservoir!

03:01.140 --> 03:02.410
Right...

03:02.410 --> 03:02.810
Kagura
Village

03:02.410 --> 03:02.810
Right...

03:02.810 --> 03:04.470
Kagura
Village

03:04.610 --> 03:06.240
And this...

03:08.950 --> 03:10.020
What is it?

03:10.020 --> 03:12.690
This might be just what we're looking for!

03:12.690 --> 03:14.290
Really?

03:14.290 --> 03:19.250
Then, they're useful, the pictures Jin took.

03:20.760 --> 03:23.460
Yes, it's a big step forward.

03:26.030 --> 03:27.660
Thank you...

04:02.300 --> 04:04.110
There isn't even any mention of it!

04:04.110 --> 04:07.010
This victim was a White Bell
member too, right?

04:08.140 --> 04:10.080
I'm not obligated to talk to the press.

04:10.080 --> 04:12.510
Hey, you jerk! I was saving that!

04:12.910 --> 04:14.020
Give that back!

04:14.020 --> 04:18.010
Aw, what a tightwad!
Making a fuss over a fried shrimp!

04:18.720 --> 04:20.980
Nobody likes a guy like that! Right?

04:21.390 --> 04:25.590
Now, you don't have to act mean
the minute you see my face!

04:28.260 --> 04:31.720
Mr. Miyamoto was such a nice man.

04:32.000 --> 04:33.000
You knew him?

04:33.000 --> 04:36.940
Yes, I met him several times
at White Bell meetings.

04:36.940 --> 04:39.410
Really? What was he like?

04:39.810 --> 04:45.040
Let's see...Even when things were hard,
he never complained.

04:50.690 --> 04:52.350
Miss Nami!

04:52.350 --> 04:53.790
Yes?

04:53.790 --> 04:59.960
Um, would you...Um, I mean...

04:59.960 --> 05:02.000
What is it?

05:02.000 --> 05:04.060
Would you go on a date with me?

05:04.170 --> 05:05.230
What?

05:05.230 --> 05:08.500
Good grief...
A little sudden, don't you think?

05:08.500 --> 05:11.370
Shut up!
In my heart, we're already connected!

05:11.370 --> 05:12.840
What's that supposed to mean?

05:12.840 --> 05:14.910
Could you just shut up for a minute?

05:14.910 --> 05:16.900
Miss Nami! Please!

05:27.090 --> 05:28.420
Sure, I will!

05:28.420 --> 05:30.090
You mean that?

05:30.090 --> 05:33.390
All right!

05:33.390 --> 05:36.530
Miss Nami, thank you! I'm so glad!

05:36.530 --> 05:37.670
Please, you're overreacting!

05:37.670 --> 05:39.400
No, no, it means a lot to me.

05:39.400 --> 05:40.070
Otomo
St. Mary's
Church
and
Children's
Center

05:40.070 --> 05:42.770
Otomo
St. Mary's
Church
and
Children's
Center

05:40.070 --> 05:42.770
Green light...

05:42.770 --> 05:43.270
Green light...

05:43.270 --> 05:44.900
Red light!

05:46.440 --> 05:49.930
Green light...Red light!

05:51.010 --> 05:53.580
Thank you, Kiriko.

05:53.580 --> 05:56.380
I got some boring paperwork done,
thanks to you.

05:56.450 --> 06:02.880
Not at all, you're always helping us out.
Besides, it takes my mind off things.

06:03.020 --> 06:04.030
Hmm?

06:04.030 --> 06:06.150
Oh, nothing!

06:07.360 --> 06:09.760
Hey! No cheating!

06:19.370 --> 06:23.580
Sorry, but could you watch the
kids just a bit longer?

06:23.580 --> 06:25.210
Huh?

06:26.580 --> 06:28.210
Sure...

06:38.090 --> 06:40.060
Hey! Running errands?

06:40.630 --> 06:42.260
Hayato!

06:46.670 --> 06:48.860
Do you remember this place?

06:50.840 --> 06:52.470
Yeah...

06:57.750 --> 07:00.770
You were nothing but trouble as a kid!

07:03.890 --> 07:07.860
After that, you started showing up
wherever I went.

07:07.860 --> 07:08.990
What?!

07:08.990 --> 07:11.520
Just like Mr. Shinjo does now!

07:12.290 --> 07:14.120
Did I really?

07:14.500 --> 07:16.190
Yes, you did!

07:22.740 --> 07:24.910
"I'm going to Tokyo."

07:24.910 --> 07:25.910
Huh?

07:25.910 --> 07:29.640
"I'll make a man of myself and
come back for you, Nami!"

07:30.350 --> 07:33.510
My heart pounded a bit
when you said that!

07:33.750 --> 07:35.910
Just a kid joking around.

07:43.260 --> 07:44.890
Of course...

07:47.300 --> 07:50.530
I had the bad dream again.

07:50.800 --> 07:54.760
The same one as always. It's terrifying!

07:55.140 --> 08:03.340
My body's floating in space, and a horrible
demon comes flying out of it!

08:05.350 --> 08:08.140
We are all equal in the eyes of God.

08:08.920 --> 08:10.220
And...

08:10.220 --> 08:11.910
That goes for God's servants too.

08:14.660 --> 08:16.280
Yes...

08:18.960 --> 08:20.460
Okay, I give up!

08:20.460 --> 08:24.470
What?! Already? What a wuss!

08:24.470 --> 08:26.090
Yeah! Yeah!

08:27.440 --> 08:31.370
All right, everyone!
It's past homework time!

08:31.640 --> 08:34.880
Shoot, I was trying not to remember.

08:34.880 --> 08:36.210
That's how it goes!

08:36.210 --> 08:38.910
All right, everyone. Let's go!

08:38.910 --> 08:41.250
Whew...Thank you.

08:41.620 --> 08:43.240
Those children...

08:43.690 --> 08:47.520
They love how you get right in
and play with them.

08:48.190 --> 08:50.560
Well, my energy's all I've got going for me.

08:50.930 --> 08:55.560
By the way, is it okay for you to be here
even though you're in the White Bell?

08:56.530 --> 08:58.560
My mother always scolds me.

08:58.770 --> 09:00.390
Oh?

09:06.010 --> 09:07.680
He sure is good!

09:07.680 --> 09:08.810
Yes...

09:08.810 --> 09:11.580
Has Father Kanzaki always lived here?

09:11.580 --> 09:16.680
Yes, but he did spend several
years in Southeast Asia.

09:17.620 --> 09:19.120
In the South Asian War?

09:19.120 --> 09:21.590
Yes, he was a chaplain.

09:21.590 --> 09:26.190
Oh, you sure know a lot
about Father Kanzaki.

09:26.590 --> 09:29.120
Not really!

09:29.460 --> 09:32.190
By the way, thank you.

09:32.770 --> 09:36.130
For bringing me my camera.

09:42.740 --> 09:45.980
There's a story about two young people...

09:46.250 --> 09:47.650
Huh?

09:47.650 --> 09:51.850
It's a folk tale the Father heard
in Southeast Asia.

09:52.320 --> 09:55.020
Kai lived in a village deep in the mountains,

09:55.020 --> 09:57.830
and she fell in love with a
traveling merchant named Hou.

09:57.830 --> 10:04.700
But the village had old, strict laws
that forbade them to marry.

10:05.500 --> 10:09.470
Kai and Hou couldn't forget each other,

10:09.470 --> 10:14.340
and they decided to leave the village
and break the rules.

10:14.340 --> 10:17.680
They promised to meet at a cave
in the mountains.

10:17.680 --> 10:21.440
Kai got there first,
and waited with bated breath.

10:21.950 --> 10:26.320
But Hou never appeared.

10:26.790 --> 10:30.320
He was ambushed by the villagers,

10:30.320 --> 10:33.360
and lost his life before he could
reach their meeting spot.

10:33.360 --> 10:36.660
Nonetheless, Hou's love for Kai

10:36.660 --> 10:41.900
took the shape of a white dove
and flew off to find her.

10:41.900 --> 10:45.010
When Kai saw what had happened,

10:45.010 --> 10:47.510
she too transformed into a white dove,

10:47.510 --> 10:52.810
and together they flew away
into the great blue sky.

10:59.390 --> 11:01.450
That's a good story.

11:01.560 --> 11:04.420
It certainly is!

11:04.760 --> 11:09.000
Oh, dear, when you get old,
you cry at the drop of the hat.

11:09.000 --> 11:10.970
Mister?

11:10.970 --> 11:13.070
It's the Father's story really.

11:13.070 --> 11:18.310
No, no, the sweet way you tell it
makes it all the more poignant!

11:18.310 --> 11:22.240
By the way, is the Father in?

11:38.190 --> 11:39.820
Here you are.

11:41.030 --> 11:42.530
Hmm...

11:42.530 --> 11:46.500
Store-bought tea, but expertly brewed.

11:46.500 --> 11:48.970
Another craft you picked up
during your time abroad?

11:50.740 --> 11:53.800
I understand you were a chaplain?

11:55.710 --> 11:58.680
Yes, it was a trial assigned to me by God.

12:00.550 --> 12:03.950
Anyway, you say you're looking for someone?

12:04.320 --> 12:08.620
Ah, yes, that's right! Over on the front lines,

12:08.620 --> 12:11.820
did you happen to encounter this woman?

12:16.030 --> 12:20.260
She's beautiful.
I'm sure I'd remember if I had.

12:20.370 --> 12:22.000
Oh?

12:22.400 --> 12:25.270
It seems I've totally missed the mark.

12:25.270 --> 12:27.880
Sorry to waste your time.

12:27.880 --> 12:29.500
Not at all.

12:30.650 --> 12:33.610
Oh, that's right! One more thing.

12:33.980 --> 12:37.490
Do you know of a joint research project
called the Gago Project,

12:37.490 --> 12:40.180
conducted by Kagura Pharmaceuticals
and the military?

12:42.390 --> 12:45.330
Was there such a thing?

12:45.330 --> 12:48.960
As a mere chaplain, I never heard of it.

12:49.200 --> 12:51.930
I see. Beg pardon!

12:51.930 --> 12:57.500
Um, would you mind telling me
a bit more about it?

12:58.470 --> 13:02.380
'Fraid I've got to get back to
scrambling for a living. See you.

13:02.380 --> 13:04.000
Of course...

13:15.220 --> 13:16.890
What was that for?!

13:16.890 --> 13:19.050
It's your own fault for sleeping there!

13:19.860 --> 13:21.100
Sheesh!

13:21.100 --> 13:24.100
Well? How'd it go at Father Kanzaki's?

13:24.100 --> 13:29.040
I had Maya pegged for a princess-type,
but she's actually really nice.

13:30.000 --> 13:32.670
You saw Maya Kuroshio at the church?

13:32.670 --> 13:35.310
Yeah! We got to be friends!

13:35.310 --> 13:37.680
And? Did you learn anything?

13:39.580 --> 13:40.580
Nope.

13:40.580 --> 13:41.380
Great.
Nope.

13:41.380 --> 13:43.050
Great.
Oh, but...

13:43.050 --> 13:45.420
I think she's in love with Father Kanzaki!

13:49.290 --> 13:51.660
I guess I'll go check it out tomorrow.

13:52.330 --> 13:56.290
The dam reservoir,
where Jin took his last picture.

13:58.670 --> 14:00.290
Okay...

14:05.540 --> 14:10.100
We haven't eaten together
as a family like this in a while!

14:10.950 --> 14:15.280
Father? I made a friend today!

14:15.480 --> 14:18.090
Oh? That's wonderful!

14:18.090 --> 14:19.720
No, it's not.

14:19.720 --> 14:23.820
Making friends at a heretic church?
It's outrageous!

14:23.820 --> 14:27.460
Now, you don't have to be so strict!

14:27.460 --> 14:33.090
You're too soft on Maya!
She's the White Bell Society priestess!

14:34.100 --> 14:37.340
Maya just wants to have friends
like anyone else!

14:37.340 --> 14:40.070
If only Tatsuo were alive!

14:41.210 --> 14:44.180
Isn't he alive?

14:44.710 --> 14:47.940
I hear he's alive and seeking revenge
as the Phantom Killer!

14:48.250 --> 14:50.010
What are you saying?!

14:50.620 --> 14:55.020
Don't worry, that's not your brother.

14:55.020 --> 14:59.460
Tatsuo died, back when you were still little.

15:00.860 --> 15:02.950
Yes, I know.

15:03.530 --> 15:10.330
Yes, Tatsuo Kagura is dead.
I suspect that phantom is...

15:12.210 --> 15:15.440
You're a bit of a mystery man, aren't you?

15:16.940 --> 15:24.520
Mr. Kuroshio wasn't on board with our vision,
but you seem to have different ideas.

15:24.520 --> 15:27.920
I'm sure the chairman has his reasons.

15:27.920 --> 15:30.690
But the younger generation
sees things differently.

15:31.030 --> 15:34.690
Oh? And you're prepared to
go through with this?

15:35.530 --> 15:40.970
I understand your patriotic motives.

15:42.500 --> 15:46.540
But do you really wield enough power?

15:46.540 --> 15:50.280
Is it money you need? Or is it Gago?

15:50.280 --> 15:53.750
That too, but more importantly...

15:53.750 --> 15:56.050
It's here, isn't it? In this town?

16:01.660 --> 16:06.720
Together, we'll pursue the dream
of a Greater East Asia!

16:17.140 --> 16:18.310
Well?

16:18.310 --> 16:19.810
That's it for sure.

16:19.810 --> 16:22.680
But it wasn't taken here.

16:22.680 --> 16:24.300
I see.

16:24.510 --> 16:26.310
What do we do?

16:26.310 --> 16:28.980
Yes, what do we do?

16:32.090 --> 16:33.750
Hey! It's you!

16:33.750 --> 16:35.920
Oh! What a coincidence!

16:35.920 --> 16:38.160
What are you doing here?

16:38.160 --> 16:41.360
Detectives always pop up unexpectedly!

16:41.360 --> 16:42.400
I'll say.

16:42.400 --> 16:44.630
I don't mean any harm.

16:44.630 --> 16:46.030
By the way...

16:46.030 --> 16:47.700
Have you heard?

16:47.700 --> 16:50.500
In Kagura Village, beneath this lake,

16:50.500 --> 16:54.130
ancient relics were discovered
the year the war ended.

16:55.510 --> 17:00.110
But all of a sudden, they abandoned
the dig right in the middle.

17:00.110 --> 17:01.120
Why?

17:01.120 --> 17:04.890
Search me. I don't know the details.

17:04.890 --> 17:06.290
Just that,

17:06.290 --> 17:10.220
rumor has it the military intervened.

17:10.490 --> 17:11.760
The military?

17:11.760 --> 17:15.130
But what exactly did they unearth?

17:15.500 --> 17:19.800
In the aftermath of the war,
that information was lost.

17:20.530 --> 17:24.210
The documents were all confiscated
by the occupying army,

17:24.210 --> 17:28.140
and the whole incident has been
shrouded in darkness.

17:28.810 --> 17:31.280
Or so it seems!

17:31.280 --> 17:32.680
Gotcha!

17:32.680 --> 17:34.710
So? How does it end?

17:37.020 --> 17:39.350
Have you heard the term "osakimochi?"

17:39.350 --> 17:40.220
What?

17:40.220 --> 17:42.920
Sounds like a kind of rice cake!

17:42.920 --> 17:47.830
In some regions they say
"osaki-sama" or "osa-kitsune..."

17:48.360 --> 17:49.990
In other words...

17:51.000 --> 17:53.600
...a house possessed by a fox spirit.

17:53.600 --> 17:55.740
I'm totally lost.

17:55.740 --> 17:58.600
Sorry, I'm not well-versed in the occult.

18:00.340 --> 18:05.610
They say there was one such house in
the village at the bottom of this lake.

18:05.610 --> 18:07.310
It belonged to...

18:07.310 --> 18:09.980
...the Kagura family!

18:20.530 --> 18:23.000
Gotcha! Ooh, this is a big one!

18:29.670 --> 18:31.470
Hey! Look!

18:37.310 --> 18:38.980
What did you see?

18:38.980 --> 18:41.970
Na-Nami...

18:50.590 --> 18:52.730
What a lovely ceremony...

18:52.730 --> 18:56.720
By the way, Tanaka, how's your daughter?

18:57.100 --> 19:00.530
We're looking forward to a
grandchild next year.

19:00.530 --> 19:03.100
Well, that's wonderful!

19:03.100 --> 19:04.870
Thank you, Sir.

19:09.640 --> 19:10.840
What was that?

19:10.840 --> 19:13.840
I'm sorry, Sir! There was a person...

19:23.490 --> 19:26.520
We owe you gentlemen a thank you.

19:27.130 --> 19:32.030
For turning us into such abominations!

19:32.630 --> 19:35.330
Lost Numbers, I presume?

19:36.740 --> 19:41.910
Bloody and guilty, guiltily awake;

19:41.910 --> 19:46.540
and in a bloody battle end thy days!

19:47.210 --> 19:51.450
The ghosts in Richard III, Act V?

19:51.450 --> 19:53.090
I read it long ago.

19:53.090 --> 19:59.050
This is a warning, Sinner.
Abandon the Gago Project.

20:00.790 --> 20:05.200
You must not bring forth
the Cocoon of Chaos.

20:07.370 --> 20:09.860
Masaki, is that you?

20:15.940 --> 20:17.950
Truly...

20:17.950 --> 20:21.140
It's like he's the ghost of Tatsuo Kagura!

20:44.940 --> 20:47.030
Your odious past...

20:49.010 --> 20:53.810
All is purified by the sound of the bell!

21:03.120 --> 21:07.800
Tatta hitotsu no sora shika nai yo

21:07.800 --> 21:12.230
Donna ni sekai ga hirokutatte

21:12.370 --> 21:16.900
Daiji na hito to hagureta toki

21:16.900 --> 21:22.500
Miageru mono ga yuukizukeru

21:22.640 --> 21:27.280
Kyou made aruite kita michi

21:27.280 --> 21:31.790
lma wa futatsu ni wakareteru

21:31.790 --> 21:40.630
Namida wa mata au hi no kokoro no shirushi

21:40.890 --> 21:45.470
Ashita wa ashita no kimi ga umareru yo

21:45.470 --> 21:50.640
Nagai yoru wo koe hi ga noboru you ni

21:50.640 --> 21:54.640
Yume no tsuzuki subete sutete

21:54.640 --> 21:58.910
Ryoute wo hirogeyou

21:59.150 --> 22:03.780
Mirai wa itsudemo kimi no me no mae de

22:03.780 --> 22:08.790
Fumidasu sono toki wo zutto matteiru

22:08.790 --> 22:12.890
Chiheisen no mukou gawa ni

22:12.890 --> 22:20.700
Mada minu sekai tsugi no deai

22:24.940 --> 22:25.010
Fear not, lost souls.

22:25.010 --> 22:28.280
Ninth Night


22:25.010 --> 22:28.280
Blessed are the Impure

22:25.010 --> 22:28.280

Fear not, lost souls.

22:28.280 --> 22:31.180
Ninth Night


22:28.280 --> 22:31.180
Blessed are the Impure

22:28.280 --> 22:31.180

Tremble not, mine heart.

22:31.180 --> 22:34.050
Ninth Night


22:31.180 --> 22:34.050
Blessed are the Impure

22:31.180 --> 22:34.050

Steep my hands and yours in blood.

22:34.050 --> 22:37.550
Ninth Night


22:34.050 --> 22:37.550
Blessed are the Impure

22:34.050 --> 22:37.550

Our day of repose lies far, far away.

22:37.550 --> 22:38.250
Ninth Night


22:37.550 --> 22:38.250
Blessed are the Impure
